# Use this Mi360 bundle

Supported: MJSXJ10CM / T31 / SC2336 / stock4.3.4_0376. Start with a rooted camera and retain its original
full-chip backup and trusted SSH access. Install Python3.12+ and SquashFS tools4.7.5 on the host.

From the extracted bundle:

```sh
BUNDLE="$PWD"
WORK="/path/to/new-private-work"
umask 077
mkdir -m 700 "$WORK"
python3 "$BUNDLE/build-image.py" --original-dump /path/to/original-dump.bin \
  --expected-original-sha256 YOUR_RECORDED_ORIGINAL_SHA256 \
  --authorized-key /path/to/key.pub --output "$WORK/native-image"
cp -R "$BUNDLE/writer" "$WORK/qualified-writer"
```

Set up [configuration](source/firmware/cameras/mi360/docs/configuration.md), then follow the bundled
[installation procedure](source/firmware/cameras/mi360/docs/install.md), starting at **Preserve the
working access path**. It stages the inactive slot and retains live DATA/settings/host keys.
The first-install procedure assumes rooted stock B is active and a stock watchdog owner is feeding;
do not apply those preconditions unchanged to an already running native installation.

Use these paths wherever that guide refers to build outputs:

| Guide input | Bundle/output path |
|---|---|
| Kernel image | `$WORK/native-image/bootstrap/kernel-for-update.bin` |
| Application image | `$WORK/native-image/B_USRFS.bin` |
| Qualified writer/updater | `$WORK/qualified-writer/{camera-mtd-write,camera-update}` |
| Environment verifier | `$BUNDLE/source/firmware/cameras/mi360/firmware/verify_environment.py` |

The writer's `plan` commands do not write flash. Staging, activation and reboot are separate explicit
steps. Stop on any failed check. The full-chip `camera-mi360-16MiB.bin` contains original private DATA
and is for a separately reviewed programmer/recovery procedure; it is not the normal updater input.

After reboot, require the same trusted SSH host key, expected active slot, attempts1 and advancing
healthy video/audio counters. Check both real streams and your configured controls.
